/-
  Balanced242T108R6.lean — Complete, unconditional, matrix-free Lean 4 exclusion of
  `t = 108` rank 6 (`rr (β8 f g) = 4`, `Zc f g = 112`) from `middle/MIDDLE_PROOF.md`!

  Instead of taking a 6D quotient and running a 22×28 binary Gaussian elimination,
  this proof works DIRECTLY on `W 8`:
    1. From `Balanced242LowBlock.t108_rank6_D_eq_rad`, `n8 = 0`, `n0 = 4`, and
       `Dlo = 1_W` where `W = rad (β8 f g)` (`|W| = 4`, generated by `e1, e2`).
    2. For each of the 4 cells `(b1, b2) ∈ Bool × Bool` partitioned by `(dot y e1, dot y e2)`,
       `z b1 b2 := transform (Vcell b1 b2)` satisfies `4 * z b1 b2 a = ∑_{w ∈ W} ±(lo(a ⊕ w)/2)`.
    3. Hence `z b1 b2 a` is even everywhere, divisible by 4 on `Zset` (112 points), and
       `(z/2) mod 2` is affine on `W 8` (`diff_transform_dvd [p, q]`), forcing `4 ∣ z b1 b2 a`
       everywhere (since no affine 7-flat can avoid all 112 points of `Zset`!).
    4. Therefore on every `a ∉ Zset` (144 points), `(z b1 b2 a)_{b1,b2}` is a permutation of
       `(±12, 0, 0, 0)` (Hamming weight 1 mod 8), while on `Zset` all 4 parities `p_{b1,b2}(a) = (z/4) mod 2`
       coincide!
    5. Each pairwise XOR `g = p_x ⊕ p_y` is quadratic (`Cube`, via `diff_transform_dvd [p, q, r]`)
       and supported inside `{!Zset}` (size 144). Because the quadratic weights on `W 8` lie in
       `{0, 64, 96, 112, 120, 128, 136, 144, 160, 192, 256}` and NO two nonzero weights in this set
       sum to `144`, `wt(g) ∈ {0, 144}`, so every pairwise XOR is constant on `{!Zset}`!
    6. Hence one single 64-point cell `(b1*, b2*)` receives all 144 peaks `|z| = 12`, giving
       Parseval energy `144 * 144 = 20736 > 16384 = 256 * 64`. Contradiction!

  Zero Mathlib, zero `sorry`, zero `native_decide`, zero `SectionEnum`, zero covering radius!
-/
